head(
## Awakening in the Manor ((+Awakening in the Manor))
)

The adventure begins with the players suddenly awakening in the foyer of the manor, disoriented and without memory of how they arrived. The air feels heavy — thick with the echoes of lullabies long forgotten and the faint scent of milk and powder.

Only one of them — the soon-to-be father — is truly here. The others are spiritual manifestations of his inner self: courage, patience, wisdom, humor, and love, given form to guide him through the trials ahead. They do not know this truth, and neither does he.

To the players, it should feel like a shared dream — vivid, uncanny, and oddly personal. The house itself reacts to the father’s emotions, twisting and changing as he faces each challenge of impending parenthood.

As they stir awake, describe the soft cry of a baby echoing through the manor — distant, pleading, familiar. The sound should pull them to their feet and toward the doors of the foyer, setting their journey in motion.

This is not an arrival. It is an awakening — and the beginning of a lesson disguised as a nightmare.


