head(
## The Foyer of Fatherhood ((+ The Foyer of Fatherhood))
)
![foyer_of_fatherhood](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/foyer-of-fatherhood.png?raw=true)

/

You awake to the sound of a cry — a single, sharp note that cuts through the veil of dreams and settles somewhere deep in your chest.  
When your eyes open, you find yourself standing in what was once a grand foyer. Long ago, it might have been a place of elegance and pride — the kind of room meant to impress guests.  
Now, it looks like it’s barely holding itself together.

Two massive, ornate doors stand before you, flanked by faded columns and crumbling trim. The walls, once polished and warm, are now caked with mysterious stains — the kind that no amount of scrubbing ever seems to remove.  
Smudged handprints, streaks of crayon, and glossy trails of dried saliva mark the surface like some chaotic mural painted by unseen little hands.

Between the grand doors looms a statue, arms outstretched as if in tribute to some unseen ruler.  
Its stone fingers clutch an offering of objects — a bottle, a rattle, a pacifier. The meaning is unmistakable: a desperate plea for appeasement.

From somewhere deeper within the manor, the cries return — louder now, sharper, echoing through the halls with unnatural resonance.  
These are no ordinary wails. There is something imperious about them, something that demands obedience.  
Each note carries the weight of a command, though what it demands of you, you cannot yet say.

Around you, several smaller doors line the room — each one a promise of mystery and danger.


 * To the **north**, a few toys lie scattered before a narrow doorway: a teddy bear, wooden blocks, a duck on a string — all perfectly still, yet somehow *watching*.  

|

 * To the **south**, books lie strewn across the floor, their pages torn and crumpled.  

A faint draft flips one open, revealing an illustration of a sleeping child — the face violently scribbled out in red crayon.


info (
## Player Prompt
This is the moment your party first awakens.  
Encourage each adventurer to describe how they react to the cry and the setting around them.  
Use this time to establish tone, introduce character quirks, and build tension before moving into exploration.

Perception check rolloff - Highest roll finds an "Elixir of Sanity" - A beer from the cooler
)

note (
## The Scene
This area sets the tone for the entire adventure — equal parts wonder and unease.  
Use environmental storytelling: distant creaks, flickering candlelight, and the echo of unseen giggles.  
Let the players feel the presence of the manor before it ever acts against them.
)

note (
## Sir Dadicus the Eternal

The lingering spirit of fatherly wisdom — and dad jokes — made manifest. Once a mortal hero of domestic responsibility, he met his end in a tragic battle against an unopened jar and its stubborn lid. His retirement plan was to finally clean out the garage, but haunting this manor seems to suit him just fine.

Sir Dadicus should be introduced while the players are in the Foyer of Fatherhood. Hint at what mechanics he has to offer.  More can be learned about Sir Dadicus in the appendix.
)




