head(
## The Toy Room ((+ The Toy Room))
### “Where Playtime Never Ends”
)

/

![toy_room](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/toy-room.png?raw=true)

/

You open the door, and chaos greets you.

The Toy Room looks as though a hurricane, an explosion, and a sugar-fueled toddler all hit at once — and maybe they did.  
The floor is a battlefield of scattered toys, overturned furniture, shredded books, and debris. Blocks, dolls, and wooden trains lie everywhere, forming treacherous piles that crunch and clatter underfoot.

And yet… this destruction doesn’t feel random.

Splintered wood and scorch marks line the walls — in several places, the damage looks eerily like actual explosions.  
A few stuffed animals hang limply from shelves or sit slumped against the wall, their fur singed and seams stretched.  
It looks like playtime ended… badly.

A massive teddy bear slumps in the corner, one button eye missing, the other gleaming faintly in the dim light.  
A wooden rocking horse stands upright but precarious, its frame creaking with each faint draft.  
Scattered across the floor, a mess of building blocks occasionally arrange themselves into short, desperate messages — words like **“Danger,” “Get Out,” “Run,”** and **“Help Me.”**  
But the moment you blink, they collapse back into meaningless piles.

An ominous weight presses down on the room, a feeling that you are not welcome here.  
The toys aren’t waiting for you — they’re waiting for someone else.  
And just as you start to consider leaving, it happens.  
The rocking horse shudders. The teddy bear’s head tilts.  
Somewhere deep within the pile of toys, something clicks to life.

*Playtime isn’t over. It’s only just begun.*

|

rules (
## Combat Encounter
The scattered toys and debris make the entire floor **difficult terrain**.  
Players may move at full speed, but must succeed at an **Athletics or Acrobatics check (DC 16)** or take **1d4 bludgeoning damage** from stepping on sharp or unstable objects.
)

note (
## Monsters
Details in the appendix
* Animated Blocks
* Lego Swarm
* Teddy Bear  
)

info (
## GM Notes
It appears that nothing here could hold the Lord Baby’s attention.  
No wonder all the toys are upset.  
Defeating or calming the toys may reveal more about the manor’s curse and the child’s restless spirit.
)


