head(
## The Nursery ((+ The Nursery))
### “The Stinker in the Shadows”
)

/

![nursery_scene](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/nursery.png?raw=true)

/

The soft flicker of a failing light greets you as you step into the nursery.  
Once a small cozy room, it now resembles a makeshift jungle gym — an overturned crib, a landing pad teddy bear, half-empty bottles, and the faint lull of a broken mobile that seems to have been used as monkey bars.

The overhead light flickers again — on… off… on… off…

At first, the room appears empty.  
But then, the smell hits you.

Something foul.  
Something sinister.  
Something that awakens the deepest primal horror of all — **the smell of a dirty diaper.**

The light cuts out completely.  
For a moment, you stand in perfect darkness, surrounded only by the faint rustle of movement and the wet pitter-patter of tiny feet on the floorboards.  

Then *click* — the light flickers back on.

Standing by the wall, one hand still on the switch, is a small gremlin wearing nothing but a swollen, sagging diaper.  
It turns its head slowly, catching you with a wide-eyed, mischievous stare — somewhere between innocence and chaos.  
The smell intensifies. The diaper looks… ready to give out.

For a brief, silent moment, you all understand the unspoken truth:  
**That diaper. Must. Be. Changed.**

The gremlin blinks. The light flickers once more.  
And then it’s gone — darting across the room at impossible speed, weaving between overturned toys and toppled furniture while still, somehow, flicking the lights off and on as it goes.

*The chase has begun.*

rules (
## The Chase
The players must catch the **Diaper Gremlin** using creative problem-solving — Athletics checks, unarmed strikes, or anything suitably chaotic.  
Each player must succeed on **3 total checks (DC 18)** to successfully corner the creature.

Once caught, they must change its diaper — represented by a **real-life blinded diaper-changing race** at the table.  
Failure results in disaster (and possibly humiliation), but success earns the gremlin’s gratitude.
)


note (
## GM Notes
Upon completion, the gremlin stands proudly, pats its freshly powdered bottom, and waddles off into the Toy Room, humming contentedly to itself.  
This scene should be played for laughs — equal parts chaos and triumph.
)


|


**Perception DC 17** to notice a faint glow coming from beneath the overturned crib.  
Amidst the clutter lies a magical baby bottle, still warm to the touch.

| Loot | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Bottle of Endless Milk** | This enchanted bottle never runs dry and can calm even the most furious of cries. Feeding it to the Lord Baby later may help quell his rage. |
| **Aeon Stone (Dusty Rose Prism)** | This aeon stone allows you to cast the 1st-rank Shield cantrip as an arcane innate spell, surrounding yourself in pink energy. The resonant power increases the damage prevented by your aeon stone's shield spell from 5 to 10. |


