head(
## The Master Bedroom ((+ The Master Bedroom))
### “Showtime before bedtime — rest is earned, not given.”
)

/

![master_bedroom](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/master-bedroom.png?raw=true)

/

You step into the Master Bedroom, and for a moment, it feels… wrong.  
Not haunted — just too clean. The bed is neatly made, the pillows fluffed, and the floorboards shine with an almost unnatural polish.  
There’s no dust, no clutter, no warmth — just the eerie sense of a room that’s barely lived in.

If it’s used at all, it can’t be for more than a few hours each night — a brief surrender to exhaustion before duty calls again.

Then you notice them.

Two small gremlins sit cross-legged on the bedspread, staring blankly at the wall.  
Their eyes are half-lidded with boredom, claws drumming rhythmically against the sheets.  
Toys lie abandoned nearby — ignored, uninteresting.  
One gremlin lets out a long, dramatic sigh before turning to you with a look of desperate expectation.

They don’t want toys.  
They want **you** to entertain them.

rules (
## Performance Challenge
The players must entertain the gremlins with any creative performance — dancing, singing, storytelling, shadow puppets, or any other inspired act.  

Use **Performance** or another **Charisma-based skill check (DC 18)**.  
Encourage the players to act it out in real life — anything genuinely funny or ridiculous earns a **+2 circumstance bonus**.

Each successful check wins the gremlins’ favor.  
Three total successes calm them and put them to sleep.  

Failure results in a brief **temper tantrum**: a wild flurry of elbows, knees, and headbutts dealing **1d4 bludgeoning damage** to a random performer.
)


|

note (
## GM Notes
The gremlins respond to the group’s energy — laughter, bad singing, or slapstick earns points.  
Let this scene breathe; it’s a lighthearted interlude amid the manor’s gloom.  
Once the players have sufficiently entertained them (3 successes), the gremlins yawn, curl up together, and fall asleep beneath the covers.

*“Doesn’t look like anyone else is getting any sleep in this bed… someone might as well use it.”*
)


**Perception DC 19** to notice the faint shimmer of light reflecting from beneath the bedframe.  
Hidden under the dust ruffle are two forgotten curiosities, gleaming faintly in the lamplight.

| Loot | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Wig of Holding** | Fashioned from planar fibers, this stylish wig conceals a small extradimensional space within its curls. It can hold up to **4 light-Bulk items** without increasing its own Bulk. Interacting with it to stow or retrieve an item requires only **one Interact action**. |
| **Mirror Robe** | Thousands of tiny mirrored shards are stitched into a long silk duster, scattering reflections across the room. While worn, you gain a subtle air of confidence — and perhaps vanity. Under bright light, the robe casts playful gleams like glittering stars. |




