head(
## The Hallway of Baby Monitors ((+ The Hallway of Baby Monitors))
)

/

The corridor hums with a wall of crackling static.  
Dozens of baby monitors sit on shelves and tables, their tiny red lights blinking in uneven rhythm.  
The noise isn’t just static — it’s *whispering*.

“You’ll never sleep again…”  
“Nap time is a lie…”  
“Rest is for the weak…”

Each monitor carries a different voice — some giggling, some sobbing, others softly cooing lullabies that twist into desperate pleas.  
As you walk, they seem to track your movement, lights flickering faster when you draw near.  
A few of them hiss louder, as if offended by your presence.  
You can’t tell whether the monitors are connected to something… or if they’re talking to each other.

The deeper you go, the more the static merges into something rhythmic — almost like breathing.  
It’s unclear whether it’s the manor, the devices, or *you* that’s exhaling now.

|

rules (
## Lingering Fear
Anyone who lingers too long among the monitors must succeed at a **Will save (DC 17)** or become **Frightened 1**, haunted by the sinking realization that the whispers might be right.  
Those who fail can almost hear their own heartbeat blending with the static, echoing in sync with the monitors’ lights.
)

note (
## GM Notes
This hallway works best as an atmospheric bridge between major encounters — a brief psychological hit before the next physical challenge.  

)




=





head(
## The Bathroom ((+ The Bathroom))
### “The Bubble Trouble”
)

/

![bathroom_scene](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/bathroom.png?raw=true)

/

The Bathroom once gleamed with motherly warmth and scented candles, but now it reeks of mildew and spilled bubble bath.  
The walls are lined with cracked tiles, their grout blackened by moisture.  
A large claw-foot tub dominates the room — its porcelain surface chipped and filled halfway with murky, bubbling water.  
Steam clings to the mirrors, which occasionally clear on their own to reveal fleeting, grinning baby faces that vanish when looked at directly.

Diapers hang like grimy flags from towel racks, and half-used bottles of bubble bath lie scattered about.  
The sink occasionally burps out foam, and every few seconds a rubber ducky can be heard squeaking somewhere nearby.

rules (
## The Encounter
When the party enters, the **door slams shut and locks magically**.  
Bubbles begin to fill the room, rising from ankle depth to chest height until visibility is nearly gone.  
Moments later, a cheerful hum echoes through the room — twisted into a discordant nursery rhyme.  
Then the foam in the tub trembles… and something **quacks**.

*Enemies:*  

* Rubber Ducky  
* Bubble Elemental

*Environmental Hazard:*  
The lingering **stench of Sir Dadicus’ visit** forces a **Fortitude save (DC 18)** or suffer the **Sickened** condition.

*Victory Condition:*  
Defeating the **Rubber Ducky** dispels the flooding magic, leaving behind a **glowing golden duck** floating serenely in the tub.  
The remaining water is absorbed into the duck’s surface, leaving behind a faint shimmer and the scent of soap.
)


## Bubble Elemental
![Bubble Elemental](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/monsters/bubble-monster.png?raw=true)


|

note (
## GM Notes
Play this scene with mounting tension that gives way to slapstick chaos.  
As the bubbles rise, make the players describe their actions — fighting blind, slipping on soap, shouting through foam.  
Let sound and smell drive the horror as much as sight.  
When the final blow lands, describe the sudden stillness — the bathwater spiraling down the drain, the rubber duck glowing like a trophy of absurd heroism.
)

**Perception DC 18** to spot a faint golden glow shimmering beneath the bubbling water.  
Fishing it out reveals the true prize — a restored relic of bath-time divinity.

