head(
## The Laundry Room ((+ The Laundry Room))
### “The Endless Cycle”
)

/

![laundry_room](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/laundry-room.png?raw=true)

/

The smell of soap hits you the moment the door creaks open.  
The Laundry Room looks like a war between order and chaos — and chaos is clearly winning.

Racks line every wall, sagging under the weight of countless baby clothes.  
Tiny shirts, onesies, bibs, and socks hang in neat, endless rows, sorted by size and color with obsessive precision.  
Each piece is spotless and perfectly folded, as if some unseen caretaker had worked tirelessly to impose control over the multitude of clothing.  
Why a baby needs so many clothes is beyond comprehension — they’re bound to grow out of them before wearing them all.

But beyond the thin veil of order lies pure mayhem.  
The floor is buried in heaps of filthy fabric — stained burp cloths, drool-soaked aprons, spoiled bedding, and blankies dragged through mud and who-knows-what.  
A sink, a wooden wash tub, and an old-fashioned washboard sit abandoned near the far wall, their surfaces crusted with dried suds.

There’s a sense that whoever tended this room fought a losing battle — scrubbing, folding, sorting, washing — until the futility of it broke them.  
Now the instruments of their work stand silent, as though the very act of doing laundry here drives the mind to ruin.

Despite the chaos, the air hums faintly, as if the room itself still expects the work to continue.  
Somewhere under the piles, you swear you hear the soft swish of fabric and the whisper of a lullaby — *“wash, rinse, repeat…”* — like a curse that refuses to end.

rules (
## Skill Challenge — “Wash, Rinse, Repeat”
Players attempt to calm the room’s restless magic by tidying the chaos with **Society**, **Crafting**, or **Performance** (or another justified skill) to “fold,” “organize,” or “soothe the magic.”  

**DC 17** checks. Track cumulative progress like a slider:  
- **Goal:** **5 total successes** before **5 total failures**.  
- **Critical Success:** The player’s neatly folded stack **stays folded** and **one nearby pile folds itself** for free (count an additional success).  
- **Failure:** An enchanted gust knocks laundry back to the floor, **adding 1 more item to fold** (count an additional failure).  
- **Critical Failure:** The chaos rattles the nerves — the performer takes a **–2 circumstance penalty on their next check**.

**Success Outcome:** The laundry piles go still, the hum softens, and a single, warm bundle remains: the **Blanket of Soothing Snuggles**.  
**Failure Outcome:** The room resets in a flurry of flying onesies; everyone is dusted in baby detergent and becomes **Fatigued** until they can clean up and rest.
)

|

note (
## GM Notes
Let players pitch creative approaches: lullabies, color-coding systems, choreographed folding, even pep talks to the piles.  
Reward genuinely funny or well-described methods with circumstance bonuses.  
Use sound to sell the scene — the cadence of the lullaby grows calmer with successes and frantic with failures.
)

**Perception DC 17** to spot a perfectly folded bundle resting atop the washer and a faint metallic gleam tucked inside a shirt pocket.

| Loot | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Blanket of Soothing Snuggles** |
| **Presentable Rune** | A garment with this rune is **always clean**, as if freshly affected by *Prestidigitation*. While wearing the presentable outfit, you gain a **+1 item bonus** to **Make an Impression** with those who’d be swayed by impeccable attire. |

