head(
## The Doctor’s Exam Room ((+ The Doctor’s Exam Room))
### “The Sniffle Plague”
)

/

![doctors_exam_room](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/doctors-exam-room.png?raw=true)

/

This room looks wrong — a sterile, clinical space inexplicably grafted into the decaying manor.  
The walls are tiled in faded white, fluorescent lights buzz faintly overhead, and the air reeks of rubbing alcohol, sour milk, and despair.

Once pristine, the surfaces are now splattered with pools of mucus and other suspicious substances, giving the floor a slick, nauseating sheen.  
Every few steps, a shoe peels up with a wet *schlorp*.  
A cracked exam table sits in the center, its paper roll long since soaked through and curling with mildew.

Scattered across the room are medical instruments and other tools — syringes, scalpels, stethoscopes — but also things that clearly don’t belong in a doctor’s office: rusty wrenches, pruning shears, a pacifier clamped in surgical forceps.  
Some still hum faintly with leftover enchantment, while others twitch or clatter when no one’s looking.

Charts and posters hang askew on the walls — anatomical drawings of infants, each one marked with runny noses and grotesquely exaggerated sinuses.  
In the back, a privacy curtain hangs half off its rail, fluttering in an unseen breeze.  
From behind it comes a soft, congested *coo*… followed by the wet sound of something sneezing.



rules (
## The Encounter — “The Sniffle Plague”
As the curtain flutters, **three Plague Zombie Babies** crawl out from beneath it.  
Their skin is blotchy and feverish gray, each one wearing a tiny hospital bracelet marked **“PATIENT ZERO.”**  
Their noses run endlessly, and their eyes gleam with sickly green light.  
When they burp or giggle, flecks of glowing bile splatter across the floor, sizzling like acid.

The moment they notice the party, they emit a chorus of **sneezes** that shake the room — filling the air with a contagious mist.

*Enemies:* Plague Baby ×3 

*Non-Combat Solution:* A **Medicine** or relevant **Recall Knowledge** check (DC 18) identifies their affliction.  
If treated with a **Medicine check (DC 19)** or other creative care (such as feeding them a potion), the babies are soothed and become non-hostile.
)


|

