## The Dining Room ((+ The Dining Room))
### “The Feast of Flinging Fools”
)

/

![dining_room](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/dining-room.png?raw=true)

/

The Dining Room once hosted lavish family dinners, but now it looks like a war zone.  
The long wooden table dominating the center of the room is buried beneath spoiled casseroles, mashed vegetables, and splattered purées in every imaginable shade of beige.  
Half-melted candles droop like stalactites, and the chandelier above drips *congealed gravy* instead of wax.

The walls are streaked with the aftermath of countless food fights — a Pollock painting of peas, carrots, and questionable baby mush.  
Rotten bread rolls litter the floor, forming soggy hazards underfoot.  
Silver platters lie overturned, and porcelain dishes hang precariously off the edges of chairs like exhausted party guests.

At the far end of the table sit **five small, wiry gremlins**, each perched in a chair as though attending a chaotic dinner party.  
Their bellies are distended, their skin slick with grease, and each guards a personal domain of filth — a mountain of mashed carrots, a sea of peas, a hill of custard, and so on.  
They hiss and chitter at the intruders, clutching spoons, ladles, and even serving forks like weapons.

Every few seconds, one scoops up a handful of goo and **flings it across the room** with gleeful precision.  
The air smells of baby food, stale mashed potatoes, and violence.

### Food Gremlin
![Food Gremlin](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/monsters/food-goblin.png?raw=true)

|

rules (
## The Food Fight
When the players enter, the gremlins immediately attack, shrieking and pelting anything that moves.  

Each gremlin has a **favorite flavor** — carrots, peas, banana, apple, and sweet potato (or whatever flavors match your real-life jars).  

**Feeding a gremlin its favorite food** pacifies it completely, turning it into a sleepy, burping lump. 

**Feeding it the wrong food** triggers a **Projectile Vomit** reaction, dealing **1d4 acid damage** to the feeder and nearby squares.

If the players pacify all five gremlins, the room falls silent except for faint snores and the drip of gravy from the chandelier.
)

note (
## Real-World Integration — The Baby Food Challenge
During this encounter, the players participate in a **real-life taste test** at the table.  
Each player samples a spoon of baby food and guesses the flavor.

**Correct guess:** Their character identifies and feeds the matching gremlin, instantly calming it.  

**Incorrect guess:** The corresponding gremlin becomes enraged and gains the **Projectile Vomit** special attack for the next round.

Encourage roleplay between bites — groans of disgust, flavor debates, and in-character taunting enhance the scene.
)

info (
## GM Notes
Use the gremlins as a mix of comedy and chaos.  
Have them taunt players by smearing food across their faces, drumming on plates, or yelling “*More!*” in unison.  
If the players fail too many guesses, have the chandelier shake loose, raining down clumps of gravy-soaked wax and forcing a **Reflex save (DC 17)** to avoid getting coated.
)

