## The Office ((+ The Office))
### “The Last Refuge”
)

/

![office_scene](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/office.png?raw=true)

/

Once, this was a sanctuary — a quiet retreat from the noise and demands of the world.  
The Office smells faintly of old coffee, warm electronics, and nostalgia.  
A heavy wooden desk dominates the room, its surface worn smooth from countless late nights of gaming, tinkering, and dreaming.  
A comfortable chair still sits behind it, turned slightly toward a computer monitor that hums softly in the dim light.

The monitor flickers — once a portal to epic adventures, fierce battles, and friendships forged through headset chatter.  
Now, it plays an endless loop of **Cocomelon**, **Ms. Rachel**, and **Bluey**, cycling without mercy.  
No buttons respond. No input changes the screen.  
The once-mighty machine has been conquered — repurposed into a shrine of catchy jingles and brightly colored torment.

Along the far wall, bookcases sag under the weight of defeat.  
Their shelves once held the finest collection of sci-fi, thrillers, and horror novels, but now the books have been pulled down and stacked into lopsided towers — makeshift building blocks for a tiny tyrant.  
Some are open, their pages smeared with crayon, applesauce, and sticky fingerprints.


|


Every available corner is crowded with toys — neon plastic creeping across the floor like an unstoppable tide.  
Rattles, blocks, and stuffed animals fill the space once reserved for thought and solitude.  
The faint sound of cheerful music leaks from the monitor — endless, inescapable, and far too cheerful to be sane.

A once-endearing refuge, now hollow.  
Like a fallen fortress.


rules (
