## The Library ((+ The Library))
### “Stories for Short Attention Spans”
)

/

![library_scene](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/library.png?raw=true)

/

The Library looks like the aftermath of a literary storm.  
Books are everywhere — stacked, toppled, flung, and abandoned mid-chapter.  
Shelves lean under the weight of half-read tomes, while the floor is buried beneath a sea of open pages and broken spines.

It’s as if someone — or something — has been trapped here in an endless cycle of distraction: pulling a book from the shelf, reading two pages, losing interest, and reaching for another.  
Again and again.  
Forever.

Many of the discarded volumes bear the evidence of this chaos — smears of food, sticky fingerprints, and the faint scent of applesauce.  
Some lie open face-down, as though mid-story tantrums froze them in time.

At the far end of the room, in front of the stained-glass bay windows, stands a single book upon a high pedestal — well beyond the reach of curious little hands.  
Its ornate script glows with a faint purple shimmer that pulses gently, like a heartbeat.


|

rules (
## Investigation
A **Perception check (DC 15)** reveals a **crumpled book** hidden beneath a pile of half-read picture books.  
