## Encounter — The Genie of Half-Read Tales
As the players approach the pedestal, the open book flares with violet light.  
The ink lifts from its pages and spirals into the air, forming a whirling cyclone of letters and punctuation.  
From within the glowing storm, a booming voice bellows:

*"At last! Someone who knows the importance of finishing a story!"*

The swirling script coalesces into a towering, indigo-skinned genie — his lower half a spiral of floating text, his grin mischievous and knowing.  
*"I am the Genie of the Half-Read Tales — guardian of literary commitment! Prove yourselves by answering my riddles, or forever remain... unfinished."*

If the players correctly answer most of his riddles, he rewards them with the **Pacifier of Blessed Silence**, muttering,  
*"Take this… It’s the only way I could get a word in while telling my tales."*
