head(
## The Boss Room ((+ The Lord of the Wails))
### “The Lord of the Wails”
)

/

![lord_of_the_wails](https://github.com/gsimon2/nightmares-of-newborn-maner/blob/main/images/scene_art/boss-room.png?raw=true)

/

You step into the heart of the manor, and the air itself trembles.  
The floor is cracked and blackened, lined with fiery fissures that pulse like a heartbeat.  
The once-grand chamber is now a battlefield of soot and ruin — the aftermath of a tantrum so powerful it tore through reality itself.

At the center of the room rises a **throne of shattered cribs and twisted toys**, precariously balanced atop a mound of splintered wood.  
Upon it sits the **Lord Baby**, pudgy fists clenched, face scrunched in pure, unfiltered rage.  
Each wail it unleashes sends a ripple of brimstone heat across the chamber.

All around the throne, tiny **goblin minions** scurry in frantic circles, desperately trying to appease their furious master.  
One offers a bottle, another shakes a rattle, a third fans the baby with a burp cloth — but nothing works.  
The cries only grow louder, angrier.  
Whatever it wants, only you can provide it.

Five glowing circles are scrawled across the floor in food stains, drool, and what you hope is finger paint.  
They pulse faintly in rhythm with the baby’s cries, flickering like the embers of a forgotten ritual.

It’s clear now — these aren’t mere markings.  
They’re **offerings**, etched from desperation.  
The house itself whispers its demand: **feed, satisfy, cleanse, comfort, and quiet.**

The walls bear the scars of countless tantrums — scorched cribs, melted bottles, toys fused to the floor.  
Each shriek shakes the rafters, a sound that feels less like crying and more like summoning.  
And yet, beneath all that fury, there’s something small and innocent — something that just wants to be held.


|

rules (
## The Final Encounter — The Lord Baby
At the center of the scorched nursery throne room sits **The Lord Baby**, radiating waves of heat, rage, and exhaustion.  
Its eyes glow with infernal fire, and every cry cracks the stone beneath your feet.

*Enemies:* **4 × Goblin Servants**

The encounter is not about destruction but **appeasement** — calming the tantrum by addressing each of the Lord Baby’s unmet needs.  
Each of the **five glowing sigils** represents one primal need.  
Placing the corresponding **relic** on a sigil satisfies that aspect and weakens the tantrum.



---

Dealing **any damage** to the Lord Baby only strengthens the tantrum.  
When struck, roll to determine which need grows louder, increasing its condition by **1 step** (Drained 2, Enfeebled 2, etc.).

The **heat aura** around the throne deals **1d4 persistent fire damage each round**.  
This can be mitigated by creativity, magic, or by using the **Rubber Ducky of Bubble Guard** to unleash its stored bathwater — cooling the room and lowering the ambient damage to **1 point per round**.
)

note (
## GM Notes
Play this encounter as equal parts epic and absurd.  
Encourage creativity and fatherly instinct over combat prowess.  
The true victory is not slaying the Lord Baby but **understanding** it — channeling patience, humor, and teamwork to survive the divine tantrum.

As each relic is placed, describe the room’s transformation:  
The fissures dim, the heat cools, the cries weaken, and the toys settle into stillness.  
)

/


