head(
# When Rage Gives Way to Rest ((+ When Rage Gives Way to Rest))
)


/

As the final offering is placed before the Lord Baby, the air grows still.



The cries that once shook the manor fade to soft coos. The fires of tantrum rage dim to a gentle, golden glow. Before your eyes, the monstrous form shrinks and softens — the horns retreat, the claws curl into tiny fingers, and what remains is a drowsy, angelic infant.



The once-mighty overlord yawns, stretches, and drifts into peaceful slumber. You step forward, instinctively — reverently — and cradle the child in your arms. For the first time since you awoke in this nightmare, the house is silent. Not the silence of dread, but of calm.



You look down at the baby’s face — serene, angelic, drooling slightly — and somehow, every trial, every mess, every horror feels… worth it. The mountains you’ve climbed now seem like ant hills. The sleepless nights, the spills, the screams — all just echoes of love in disguise.



A small smile creeps across your face. You wouldn’t change a thing.You feel a gentle hand rest upon your shoulder. Turning back, you see your companions smiling — warm, proud, and slowly fading into the soft light around you.



It’s then you understand: they were never just fellow adventurers, but reflections of what you’ll need for the road ahead — strength to endure, resilience to rise again, knowledge to guide you, patience to listen, and love to see it through.



Though their forms dissolve like mist at dawn, their presence lingers — not gone, only waiting. And when the next challenge comes, when the cries return and the nights grow long… they will be there, as they always were.



The darkness doesn’t brighten, but the shadows feel softer now. The mess remains, but it no longer feels like ruin — it echoes with the memories of playtime. The chaos endures, but it’s yours. A reminder of the life, the noise, the love that fills your world.



Your peaceful, sleeping, beautiful little world…



At least until they get hungry again.




=


